cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FlyGPT
message: >-
  If you use this software or artifacts derived from it, please cite it
  as below, and cite the upstream connectome datasets listed under
  references.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-01-01' # placeholder - update at first tagged release
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - name: FlyGPT contributors
abstract: >-
  FlyGPT is, to our knowledge, the first trained generative model of a
  complete synapse-resolution connectome's dynamics: a transformer
  trained on simulated leaky-integrate-and-fire dynamics of the male
  fruit-fly central nervous system connectome, with a female-conditioned
  branch on the BANC connectome.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - foundation model
  - neural dynamics
  - transformer
repository-code: https://github.com/flygpt/flygpt
url: https://huggingface.co/flygpt
references:
  - type: article
    scope: "MaleCNS v1.0 connectome dataset (primary training graph)"
    title: "A connectome of the male Drosophila central nervous system"
    authors:
      - family-names: Berg
        given-names: "S."
      - name: "MaleCNS Consortium"
    journal: Cell
    year: 2026
    notes: "Janelia FlyEM, University of Cambridge, Google. Data CC-BY-4.0, gs://flyem-male-cns/v1.0/"
  - type: article
    scope: "BANC female brain-and-nerve-cord connectome (sex-conditioning branch)"
    title: "Comparative connectomics of the Drosophila brain and nerve cord"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bates
        given-names: "A. S."
      - family-names: Phelps
        given-names: "J. S."
      - family-names: Kim
        given-names: "S. S."
    journal: Nature
    year: 2026
    notes: "Data CC-BY-4.0"
  - type: article
